<title>JAPAN: Jet fuel pipelines to Tokyo airport back on line.</title>
<headline>Jet fuel pipelines to Tokyo airport back on line.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pipelines supplying jet fuel to Tokyo's Narita airport, which were automatically cut off as a safety measure after a strong earthquake on Wednesday, resumed operations on Friday morning, an airport official said.</p>
<p>Two pipelines running 47 km between an oil terminal at Chiba port and the airport were shut when an earthquake measuring 6.6 on the Richter scale hit Tokyo and surrounding areas late on Wednesday morning.</p>
<p>The airport had about 90,000 kilolitres of jet fuel stocks, enough for about seven days, when the pipelines were closed.</p>
</text>
